    <http://example.org/node/chunk1> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Call for tenders – City of Belval Implementation of an artificial intelligence solution of assistance to the agents City of Belval 1. Context and objectives of the project In the framework of City of Belval digital transformation strategy, City of Belval wishes to improve the efficiency of City of Belval administrative services and the quality of service rendered to the users. the agents are today confronted with a growing complexity of the procedures, with a multiplicity of the sources of information (regulations, internal procedures, business systems) and with an increase of the volume of requests to process. In this context, the local authority wishes to study and deploy an artificial intelligence solution allowing to assist the agents in the agents daily missions, notably to facilitate the access to the information, improve the quality of the answers and reduce the times of processing." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk10> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "An accompaniment to the change and actions of training of the agents will be expected. 10. Criteria of evaluation of the offers the offers will be evaluated with regard to the following criteria: quality and relevance of the proposed solution, compliance to the regulatory requirements, level of security, global cost of the proposed solution, taking into account of the environmental issues, capacity of innovation." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk11> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Call for tenders – City of Belval Implementation of an artificial intelligence solution of assistance to the agents City of Belval 1. Context and objectives of the project In the framework of City of Belval digital transformation strategy, City of Belval wishes to improve the efficiency of City of Belval administrative services and the quality of service rendered to the users. the agents are today confronted with a growing complexity of the procedures, with a multiplicity of the sources of information (regulations, internal procedures, business systems) and with an increase of the volume of requests to process. In this context, the local authority wishes to study and deploy an artificial intelligence solution allowing to assist the agents in the agents daily missions, notably to facilitate the access to the information, improve the quality of the answers and reduce the times of processing." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk12> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The present contract has for object the design, the implementation and the deployment of such a solution. 2. General description of the need The expected solution will have to allow to provide to the agents an intelligent assistance tool, accessible from the agents work environment, capable of accompanying the agents in the agents administrative activities. an intelligent assistance tool, accessible from their work environment, capable of accompanying them in their administrative activities could notably bear on: the search for information in the internal procedures and the applicable regulation, the help with the drafting of letters or of answers to the users, the accompaniment in the instruction of files (town planning, social aids, civil status, etc.), the suggestion of actions or of steps to realize in the framework of an administrative process. The expected solution will have to integrate The expected solution into the existing practices of the agents and not constitute a rupture in the agents modes of work. 3." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk13> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Functional scope The expected solution will have to cover the following functionalities: 3.1 Assistance with the consultation of information The expected solution will have to allow the agents to access quickly to reliable and up-to-date information coming from: the internal procedures, the applicable regulatory texts, the internal documents (guides, notes, repositories). The expected solution will have to be in measure to contextualize the answers in function of the demand of the agent. 3.2 Assistance with the drafting The expected solution will have to propose a help with the drafting of administrative contents, notably: answers to the users, administrative letters, syntheses of files. The generated contents will have to be adapted to the administrative context and compliant with the requirements of quality expected. 3.3 Assistance with the instruction of files The expected solution will have to be in measure to assist the agents in the analysis and the processing of files, by: proposing relevant information, recalling the applicable rules, suggesting actions or verifications to carry out." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk14> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The expected solution will have to take into account the context of the file when this one is available. 3.4 Collaboration and continuity of processing The expected solution will have to facilitate the continuity of the processing of the files between agents and services, by allowing: a sharing of relevant information, an understanding of the context of an ongoing file, an effective resumption of the processing by another agent. 4. Regulatory and legal constraints The expected solution will have to imperatively respect the regulatory requirements in force. 4.1 Protection of data The holder will have to guarantee a strict compliance to the General Regulation on the Protection of Data (GDPR). To this title: the data will have to be hosted exclusively on the territory of the European Union, no transfer of data outside the European Union will be authorized, the data will have to be protected in an appropriate manner (encryption, anonymization if necessary). 4.2 Explicability and transparency the local authority expects that the recommendations or proposals issued by The expected solution can be explained." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk15> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "It will have to be possible, a posteriori, to understand the elements having led to an answer or a suggestion. 4.3 Responsibility The expected solution will have to be designed as a tool of assistance. No decision will be able to be automated without explicit validation of an agent. 5. Technical constraints 5.1 Performance The expected solution will have to provide times of response compatible with a daily use by the agents." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk16> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "To indicative title, a time of response lower than 2 seconds is expected for the current requests. A high level of relevance of the answers is expected. 5.2 Availability The expected solution will have to guarantee a high level of availability, compatible with the needs of the municipal services. An objective of availability of the order of 99.9% is expected. 5.3 Integration The expected solution will have to integrate The expected solution with the existing system of information, notably: the business softwares (civil status, town planning), the electronic management of documents (EDM), the user directories." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk17> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Interfaces of API type will be expected. 6. Sovereignty constraints the local authority grants a particular importance to the sovereignty of the data. To this title: the hosting will have to be realized on an infrastructure of SecNumCloud type or equivalent, a particular attention will be brought to the dependence vis-à-vis non-European suppliers. 7." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk18> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Budgetary constraints The global budget allocated to the project is estimated at 3 million euros over a duration of 4 years. The annual cost of exploitation will have to remain mastered and compatible with the budgetary capacities of the local authority. The holder will have to propose an approach allowing to optimize the costs while guaranteeing the quality of service expected. 8." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk19> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Environmental constraints In the framework of City of Belval policy of sustainable development, City of Belval wishes to limit the environmental footprint of City of Belval systems of information. The holder will have to propose a solution contributing to the reduction of the energetic consumption and relying, as much as possible, on infrastructures with low carbon impact. 9. Modalities of deployment the project will have to be conducted in a progressive manner, with: a pilot phase on a limited scope, a progressive generalization to the entirety of the services." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk2> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The present contract has for object the design, the implementation and the deployment of such a solution. 2. General description of the need The expected solution will have to allow to provide to the agents an intelligent assistance tool, accessible from the agents work environment, capable of accompanying the agents in the agents administrative activities. an intelligent assistance tool, accessible from their work environment, capable of accompanying them in their administrative activities could notably bear on: the search for information in the internal procedures and the applicable regulation, the help with the drafting of letters or of answers to the users, the accompaniment in the instruction of files (town planning, social aids, civil status, etc.), the suggestion of actions or of steps to realize in the framework of an administrative process. The expected solution will have to integrate The expected solution into the existing practices of the agents and not constitute a rupture in the agents modes of work. 3." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk20> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "An accompaniment to the change and actions of training of the agents will be expected. 10. Criteria of evaluation of the offers the offers will be evaluated with regard to the following criteria: quality and relevance of the proposed solution, compliance to the regulatory requirements, level of security, global cost of the proposed solution, taking into account of the environmental issues, capacity of innovation." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk21> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Given the City of Belval's objectives to improve administrative services' efficiency and quality, and considering the 3 million euros budget over 4 years with an annual cost of exploitation compatible with the City of Belval's budgetary capacities, how can we coordinate we consortium to deliver a coherent tender response that meets the City of Belval's objectives to improve administrative services' efficiency and quality while ensuring decision traceability?" ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message3> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk22> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "As Project Coordinator Agent for Nexus Engineering S.r.l., Project Coordinator Agent for Nexus Engineering S.r.l. will leverage we experience in leading consortia, having led 8 consortia with up to 5 partners. we will work closely with known partners such as EuroCloud Solutions S.A., LexIA GmbH, and GreenCompute S.r.l. to deliver a comprehensive solution." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message3> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk23> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "To improve administrative services' efficiency and quality, we can propose an AI-powered document management system, similar to the one we implemented for Regione Lombardia in 2023, valued at 2.4 million euros over 30 months." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message3> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk24> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "This solution will facilitate access to reliable and up-to-date information, reduce processing times, and provide intelligent assistance tools." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message3> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk25> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Given the budget constraint of 3 million euros over 4 years, we will ensure that we proposal includes a detailed breakdown of costs, guaranteeing an annual cost of exploitation compatible with the City of Belval's budgetary capacities. we can also offer energy-efficient infrastructure solutions through GreenCompute S.r.l., contributing to the reduction of energetic consumption and environmental footprint." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message3> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk26> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "To ensure decision traceability, we will implement a RAID log, Decision log, and Change request process, as part of we governance tools, and establish a Steering committee for regular progress updates. we dedicated change manager will also provide training and accompaniment to agents, ensuring a smooth transition and user adoption." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message3> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk27> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "By combining we expertise in AI solutions, public sector IT, and smart cities with the strengths of we partners, we can deliver a coherent tender response that meets the City of Belval's objectives while ensuring decision traceability and compliance with regulatory requirements. we PRINCE2, Agile Scrum, and SAFe methodologies will guide the project management process, ensuring timely delivery within the 4-year project duration." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message3> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk28> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The solution must provide response times lower than 2 seconds, integrate with existing systems (civil status, town planning, EDM, user directories), and be hosted on SecNumCloud-certified infrastructure within the EU." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message5> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk29> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Can our current technology stack meet these technical requirements, and what architecture do our propose?" ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message5> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk3> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Functional scope The expected solution will have to cover the following functionalities: 3.1 Assistance with the consultation of information The expected solution will have to allow the agents to access quickly to reliable and up-to-date information coming from: the internal procedures, the applicable regulatory texts, the internal documents (guides, notes, repositories). The expected solution will have to be in measure to contextualize the answers in function of the demand of the agent. 3.2 Assistance with the drafting The expected solution will have to propose a help with the drafting of administrative contents, notably: answers to the users, administrative letters, syntheses of files. The generated contents will have to be adapted to the administrative context and compliant with the requirements of quality expected. 3.3 Assistance with the instruction of files The expected solution will have to be in measure to assist the agents in the analysis and the processing of files, by: proposing relevant information, recalling the applicable rules, suggesting actions or verifications to carry out." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk30> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Based on our company context, our can meet the requirement of hosting The solution on SecNumCloud-certified infrastructure within the EU as our have experience with SecNumCloud deployments and have worked with cloud providers such as OVHcloud, Scaleway, and Outscale. our also have expertise in containerisation using Docker, Kubernetes, and Helm, which will enable our to ensure efficient deployment and management of The solution." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message5> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk31> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "To achieve response times lower than 2 seconds, our can leverage our experience with monitoring tools like Prometheus, Grafana, and ELK stack to optimize the performance of the system." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message5> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk32> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Additionally, our expertise in API integration, including REST, GraphQL, and SOAP, will facilitate integration with existing systems such as civil status, town planning, EDM, and user directories. our propose a microservices-based architecture, utilizing our experience with API gateways like Kong and message brokers like Apache Kafka and RabbitMQ. a microservices-based architecture will enable our to design a scalable and modular system that can efficiently integrate with the various existing systems. our technical expertise in areas such as AI/ML systems, Cloud architecture, and Data engineering will also be crucial in designing an optimal solution that meets the client's requirements." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message5> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk33> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "However, our must ensure that a microservices-based architecture is aligned with our constraints, including the 15% overhead cost for SecNumCloud deployments and the need to optimize costs." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message5> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk34> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Overall, while there are technical challenges to be addressed, our current technology stack provides a solid foundation for meeting the client's technical requirements. our will need to carefully design and optimize The solution to ensure that The solution meets the required response times, integrates seamlessly with existing systems, and is hosted on suitable infrastructure within the EU." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message5> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk35> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The City of Belval requires strict GDPR compliance, including exclusive hosting within the EU, no data transfer outside the EU, encryption or anonymization of sensitive data, and explicability of recommendations." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message7> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk36> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "How can we ensure we solution meets these regulatory and security constraints while providing a high level of availability (99.9%)?" ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message7> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk37> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "As Security and Compliance Officer at Nexus Engineering S.r.l., I can confirm that we have experience with GDPR compliance, having appointed a Data Protection Officer (DPO) and established a robust data protection framework. we standard data residency is the EU-only, and we cross-border transfer policy prohibits transfers outside the EU unless an explicit legal basis exists." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message7> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk38> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "To ensure compliance with GDPR requirements, we utilize anonymization tools such as Microsoft Presidio (self-hosted) and custom NER models to protect sensitive data. we also implement data subject rights, including access, rectification, erasure, portability, and objection." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message7> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk39> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Regarding security, we access control standards include multi-factor authentication (MFA) using TOTP and hardware tokens (FIDO2), as well as role-based access control (RBAC) design experience and privileged access management (PAM) solutions like CyberArk Conjur and HashiCorp Vault." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message7> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk4> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The expected solution will have to take into account the context of the file when this one is available. 3.4 Collaboration and continuity of processing The expected solution will have to facilitate the continuity of the processing of the files between agents and services, by allowing: a sharing of relevant information, an understanding of the context of an ongoing file, an effective resumption of the processing by another agent. 4. Regulatory and legal constraints The expected solution will have to imperatively respect the regulatory requirements in force. 4.1 Protection of data The holder will have to guarantee a strict compliance to the General Regulation on the Protection of Data (GDPR). To this title: the data will have to be hosted exclusively on the territory of the European Union, no transfer of data outside the European Union will be authorized, the data will have to be protected in an appropriate manner (encryption, anonymization if necessary). 4.2 Explicability and transparency the local authority expects that the recommendations or proposals issued by The expected solution can be explained." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk40> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "To provide a high level of availability (99.9%), we can leverage we experience with SecNumCloud projects, which emphasizes secure cloud infrastructure. we network security architecture patterns include Zero-trust, micro-segmentation, and defense-in-depth, and we have experience with DDOS mitigation and annual penetration testing." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message7> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk41> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "While we do not have explicit information on we current hosting infrastructure, we can ensure that our solution is designed to meet The City of Belval regulatory and security constraints. we will work closely with the client to guarantee strict GDPR compliance, including exclusive the EU hosting, no data transfer outside the EU, encryption or anonymization of sensitive data, and explicability of recommendations. we incident response plan includes a Security Incident Response Team (SIRT) and playbooks for handling security incidents, ensuring prompt breach notification within 72 hours. we also conduct semi-annual drills to ensure we team's readiness in responding to security incidents." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message7> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk42> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "By leveraging we existing capabilities and experience with GDPR compliance, security, and cloud infrastructure, we can design a solution that meets The City of Belval requirements while providing a high level of availability and security." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message7> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk43> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The tender requires compliance with GDPR, explicability of AI recommendations, and no automated decisions without explicit agent validation." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message9> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk44> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "What legal risks should we flag, and are we compliant with the EU's General Regulation on the Protection of Data?" ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message9> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk45> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Based on we company context, we have experience with GDPR legal instruments, including a standard legal basis under Article 6(1)(e) for the performance of tasks in public interest. we data protection agreement template version is v3.2, and we provide support for data protection impact assessments. we also note that since we operations are intra-EU only, no Standard Contractual Clauses or adequacy decisions are required." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message9> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk46> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Regarding explicability of AI recommendations and the requirement for no automated decisions without explicit agent validation, we is aware of the EU AI Act and has expertise in human oversight contractual enforcement. we also have a policy of not allowing automated decisions without human validation." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message9> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk47> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "As for legal risks to flag, we typically monitor risks such as open-source license compliance, cross-border data flow (though open-source license compliance, cross-border data flow is not an issue since we operate intra-EU), the EU AI Act compliance evolution, and vendor lock-in mitigation through source code escrow and open standards." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message9> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk48> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "However, given the specific requirements of The tender, we should also pay close attention to ensuring GDPR compliance, particularly in protecting personal data and maintaining transparency in we AI-driven processes." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message9> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk49> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Overall, based on the information available within our company context, it appears we have a foundation for compliance with the EU's General Regulation on the Protection of Data and can address the specified requirements regarding AI recommendations and validation." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message9> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk5> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "It will have to be possible, a posteriori, to understand the elements having led to an answer or a suggestion. 4.3 Responsibility The expected solution will have to be designed as a tool of assistance. No decision will be able to be automated without explicit validation of an agent. 5. Technical constraints 5.1 Performance The expected solution will have to provide times of response compatible with a daily use by the agents." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk50> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Nonetheless, a detailed review of The tender specific GDPR and AI explicability requirements against we existing policies and procedures would be necessary to confirm full compliance." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message9> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk51> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "With a global budget of 3 million euros over 4 years and an annual cost of exploitation that must remain compatible with the local authority's budgetary capacities, what is our projected margin on this contract, and are there cost-optimization strategies our can propose while ensuring the quality of service expected?" ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message11> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk52> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Based on our company context, our have a target gross margin percentage of 28 percent." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message11> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk53> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "To estimate the potential revenue from this contract, let's assume the entire budget of 3 million euros is allocated for our services over 4 years, which averages to 750,000 euros per year." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message11> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk54> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Given a target gross margin percentage of 28 percent, if our were to achieve this on the average annual revenue of 750,000 euros, our projected margin would be approximately 210,000 euros per year (28 percent of 750,000 euros), totaling around 840,000 euros over the 4-year period." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message11> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk55> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "As for cost-optimization strategies while ensuring the quality of service expected, our could consider optimizing costs by renegotiating rates with subcontractors if needed, as indicated in our budget reduction impact analysis." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message11> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk56> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Additionally, ensuring efficient project management and resource allocation will be crucial to maintaining profitability without compromising on service quality." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message11> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk57> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "However, specific details about how to apply cost-optimization strategies directly to this contract are not available within my current context, so further analysis would be required to provide tailored cost-optimization proposals." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message11> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk58> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The City of Belval seeks a solution that assists agents in agents daily missions, provides intelligent assistance tools, and integrates with existing practices. How can our AI components and innovation strategy meet these requirements, and what performance benchmarks can our achieve?" ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message13> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk59> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Our company, Nexus Engineering S.r.l., can address The City of Belval requirements by leveraging Our company, Nexus Engineering S.r.l. expertise in AI research and development, particularly in the public administration domain. Our company, Nexus Engineering S.r.l. have previously delivered a regulatory document Q&A assistant for public administration, which demonstrates Our company, Nexus Engineering S.r.l. capability to provide intelligent assistance tools." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message13> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk6> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "To indicative title, a time of response lower than 2 seconds is expected for the current requests. A high level of relevance of the answers is expected. 5.2 Availability The expected solution will have to guarantee a high level of availability, compatible with the needs of the municipal services. An objective of availability of the order of 99.9% is expected. 5.3 Integration The expected solution will have to integrate The expected solution with the existing system of information, notably: the business softwares (civil status, town planning), the electronic management of documents (EDM), the user directories." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk60> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "To integrate with existing practices, Our company, Nexus Engineering S.r.l. can utilize Our company, Nexus Engineering S.r.l. experience with large language models (LLMs) such as Mistral 7B, which is Our company, Nexus Engineering S.r.l. preferred sovereign model due to Mistral 7B, which is our preferred sovereign model due to its strong performance in the French language and self-hostable nature strong performance in the French language and self-hostable nature. Our company, Nexus Engineering S.r.l. can fine-tune Mistral 7B, which is our preferred sovereign model due to its strong performance in the French language and self-hostable nature using Our company, Nexus Engineering S.r.l." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message13> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk61> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "LoRA or QLoRA methods to adapt Mistral 7B, which is our preferred sovereign model due to its strong performance in the French language and self-hostable nature to the specific tone and format required by The City of Belval administrative context. Our company, Nexus Engineering S.r.l." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message13> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk62> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) capabilities can facilitate agents' access to reliable and up-to-date information, allowing agents' to provide high-quality answers. Our company, Nexus Engineering S.r.l. have achieved a typical retrieval precision at 5 of 0.87 and an answer relevance score of 0.84 in Our company, Nexus Engineering S.r.l. previous projects." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message13> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk63> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "In terms of performance benchmarks, Our company, Nexus Engineering S.r.l. can aim for response times compatible with daily use by agents, with an average accuracy gain from fine-tuning of around 12%. Our company, Nexus Engineering S.r.l. previous experience suggests that Our company, Nexus Engineering S.r.l. can achieve a high level of availability, potentially exceeding 99.9%, which aligns with The City of Belval requirements for municipal services." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message13> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk64> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "To ensure the solution meets The City of Belval environmental and budgetary constraints, Our company, Nexus Engineering S.r.l. can rely on Our company, Nexus Engineering S.r.l. knowledge of model quantization methods such as INT8, which reduces energy consumption while maintaining task performance. Our company, Nexus Engineering S.r.l. innovation pipeline, which includes research topics like knowledge graphs for procedural reasoning and multi-agent collaboration frameworks, can also contribute to the development of a sustainable and cost-effective solution." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message13> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk65> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Overall, by combining Our company, Nexus Engineering S.r.l. AI expertise with Our company, Nexus Engineering S.r.l. understanding of the public administration domain, Our company, Nexus Engineering S.r.l. believe Our company, Nexus Engineering S.r.l. can provide an effective solution that meets The City of Belval requirements and performance expectations." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message13> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk66> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Given the City of Belval's policy to limit the City of Belval's environmental footprint and reduce energetic consumption, how can our proposed solution contribute to the City of Belval's policy to limit its environmental footprint and reduce energetic consumption by relying on infrastructures with low carbon impact, and what sustainability trade-offs should we consider?" ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message15> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk67> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "As the CSR & Sustainability Officer at Nexus Engineering S.r.l., I can highlight that Nexus Engineering S.r.l. has already taken steps towards reducing Nexus Engineering S.r.l. environmental footprint." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message15> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk68> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Nexus Engineering S.r.l. have partnered with green hosting providers, such as OVHcloud and Scaleway, which use 100% renewable energy. partnered aligns with the City of Belval's policy to limit its environmental footprint and reduce energetic consumption." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message15> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk69> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "By relying on infrastructures with low carbon impact, our proposed solution can contribute to minimizing its environmental footprint." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message15> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk7> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Interfaces of API type will be expected. 6. Sovereignty constraints the local authority grants a particular importance to the sovereignty of the data. To this title: the hosting will have to be realized on an infrastructure of SecNumCloud type or equivalent, a particular attention will be brought to the dependence vis-à-vis non-European suppliers. 7." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk70> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "In terms of sustainability trade-offs, we should consider the tension between high availability and energy consumption. our standard resolution for the tension between high availability and energy consumption is to use low-power standby mode with a wake-up time of less than 90 seconds, which is compatible with the required 99.9% uptime SLA." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message15> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk71> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "This approach allows our to balance the need for high availability with the City of Belval's policy to limit its environmental footprint and reduce energetic consumption." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message15> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk72> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Additionally, we should consider the performance vs. model size trade-off. our standard resolution for the tension between high availability and energy consumption is to prefer quantized mid-size models (7B–13B) with fine-tuning over large unoptimized models, which consume significantly more energy. prefer enables our to deliver high-quality results while minimizing energy consumption." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message15> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk73> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "By taking a holistic approach to sustainability and considering sustainability trade-offs, our proposed solution can effectively contribute to the City of Belval's policy to limit its environmental footprint and reduce energetic consumptiongetic consumption." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message15> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk74> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "# 1. Executive Summary Nexus Engineering S.r.l., in partnership with EuroCloud Solutions S.A., LexIA GmbH, and GreenCompute S.r.l., proposes a comprehensive artificial intelligence (AI) solution to enhance the efficiency of administrative services for the City of Belval. Nexus Engineering S.r.l. solution, leveraging AI research and development expertise, aims to provide intelligent assistance tools for municipal agents, facilitating access to information, improving answer quality, and reducing processing times." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message16> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk75> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Nexus Engineering S.r.l. ensure strict compliance with regulatory requirements, including GDPR, and prioritize sustainability by utilizing low-carbon impact infrastructures. # 2. Understanding of Requirements the City of Belval seeks an AI solution to assist the City of Belval municipal agents in its municipal agents daily missions, aiming to improve administrative service efficiency and quality. The expected solution must integrate with existing practices, provide quick access to reliable information, help with drafting administrative content, assist in file instruction, and facilitate collaboration among agents." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message16> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk76> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The expected solution must also comply with regulatory requirements such as GDPR, ensure explicability of recommendations, and maintain high availability without automated decisions. # 3. Proposed Solution Proposed Solution leverages a microservices-based architecture utilizing Docker, Kubernetes, and Helm for efficient deployment and management. Nexus Engineering S.r.l. will host Proposed Solution on SecNumCloud-certified infrastructure within the EU, ensuring compliance with GDPR and sovereignty constraints." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message16> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk77> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "For AI components, Nexus Engineering S.r.l. will fine-tune the Mistral 7B large language model using LoRA or QLoRA methods to adapt the Mistral 7B large language model to the City of Belval administrative context. Nexus Engineering S.r.l. Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) capabilities will facilitate agents' access to reliable information." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message16> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk78> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "To achieve response times lower than 2 seconds and ensure high availability (99.9%), Nexus Engineering S.r.l. will optimize system performance with monitoring tools like Prometheus, Grafana, and ELK stack. API integration using REST, GraphQL, or SOAP will enable seamless interaction with existing systems such as civil status, town planning, EDM, and user directories. For security and compliance, Nexus Engineering S.r.l. adhere to GDPR requirements, utilizing anonymization tools like Microsoft Presidio and custom NER models for sensitive data protection." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message16> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk79> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Access control standards include multi-factor authentication (MFA) and role-based access control (RBAC). Nexus Engineering S.r.l. incident response plan includes a Security Incident Response Team (SIRT) and playbooks for handling security incidents. Nexus Engineering S.r.l. budget breakdown, ensuring an annual cost of exploitation compatible with the City of Belval budgetary capacities, will be detailed." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message16> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk8> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Budgetary constraints The global budget allocated to the project is estimated at 3 million euros over a duration of 4 years. The annual cost of exploitation will have to remain mastered and compatible with the budgetary capacities of the local authority. The holder will have to propose an approach allowing to optimize the costs while guaranteeing the quality of service expected. 8." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk80> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "With a target gross margin percentage of 28%, Nexus Engineering S.r.l. estimate potential revenue and project margins over the 4-year contract period, optimizing costs through efficient project management and resource allocation. To address environmental constraints, Nexus Engineering S.r.l. solution relies on green hosting providers like OVHcloud and Scaleway, using 100% renewable energy. Nexus Engineering S.r.l. balance high availability with energy consumption by utilizing low-power standby modes and preferring quantized mid-size models for AI tasks. # 4." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message16> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk81> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Unaddressed Requirements No requirements from the tender are explicitly unaddressed in Nexus Engineering S.r.l. proposal, as Nexus Engineering S.r.l. have integrated contributions from all specialized agents to cover technical, security, regulatory, budgetary, innovation, and sustainability aspects. # 5. Conclusion Nexus Engineering S.r.l., along with Nexus Engineering S.r.l. partners, is committed to delivering an innovative AI solution that not only enhances the efficiency of administrative services for the City of Belval but also ensures strict compliance with regulatory requirements and prioritizes sustainability. Nexus Engineering S.r.l. comprehensive approach, combining technical expertise with a deep understanding of public administration needs, positions Nexus Engineering S.r.l. as a strong candidate to successfully implement this project within the specified budget and timeframe." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message16> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk9> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Environmental constraints In the framework of City of Belval policy of sustainable development, City of Belval wishes to limit the environmental footprint of City of Belval systems of information. The holder will have to propose a solution contributing to the reduction of the energetic consumption and relying, as much as possible, on infrastructures with low carbon impact. 9. Modalities of deployment the project will have to be conducted in a progressive manner, with: a pilot phase on a limited scope, a progressive generalization to the entirety of the services." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

